[{"id": "fb230c1", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "5705b30", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "shortcode", "settings": {"shortcode": "[rank_math_breadcrumb]"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "8ddaf49", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "How to trim your dog's nails", "header_size": "h1"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e7e34c7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You want to keep your dog's nails short without hitting the quick, the sensitive part inside the nail, and know what to do if a nail bleeds.</p>", "typography_typography": "custom", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "10897ea", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>By Grooming Dogs · Updated {{UPDATED}}</p>", "text_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9da819c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ul><li><strong>How often to trim:</strong> see <a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\">how often to trim nails</a>.</li><li><strong>If your dog panics or pulls away:</strong> start with <a href=\"/grooming-an-anxious-dog/\">if your dog won't let you</a>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "820459b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "image", "settings": {"image": {"id": 31, "url": "https://grooming-dogs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/pexels-photo-19145872.jpeg", "alt": "A groomer gently supporting a dog's front paw while holding a pair of dog nail clippers.", "source": "library"}, "image_size": "large", "caption_source": "custom", "caption": "Photo: Goochie Poochie Grooming / Pexels", "caption_typography_typography": "custom", "caption_color": "#5B6870", "__globals__": {"caption_typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=accent", "caption_color": "globals/colors?id=secondary"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "958b5f2", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}}, "elements": [{"id": "c5578f3", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Short answer:</strong></p>\n<ol><li><strong>Hold the toe gently</strong> so the nail extends.</li><li><strong>Clip only the tip, straight across,</strong> taking small amounts <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Stop before the quick.</strong> On light nails it's the pink area. On dark nails, stop when the cut end shows a chalky ring or a shiny, moist-looking center <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>If you nick the quick,</strong> press styptic powder or cornstarch onto the tip <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>. If the bleeding hasn't stopped after a few minutes, call your vet <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>For very long nails,</strong> trim a little at a time rather than all at once <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li></ol>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "ec0273d", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "03a65c6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Why nail length matters", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "why-nail-length-matters"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "2a06220", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Nails that grow too long can cause problems:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Movement:</strong> long nails can affect how your dog walks and places their feet <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Discomfort and breakage:</strong> they can cause discomfort and make broken nails more likely <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Snagging:</strong> a long nail can catch on something like carpet and break, which is painful and can bleed <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Feet and legs over time:</strong> over a long period, overgrown nails can change the shape of the foot and strain the leg <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "8eae36c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Signs a trim is due:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>you can hear the nails clicking on hard floors <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>;</li><li>the nails nearly touch the ground when your dog walks <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "6fdd554", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>How often that happens depends on your dog. See <a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\">how often to trim nails</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "bd2c18d", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "ddbaace", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Finding the quick", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "finding-the-quick"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "404bef7", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>The quick is the living core of the nail. It carries blood vessels and nerves, so cutting into it hurts and makes the nail bleed <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "96e7f0b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Light-colored nails", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "d829599", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>On white or clear nails, you can see the quick as a pink area inside the nail <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. Clip the nail tip well short of the pink.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1eaaa95", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Black nails", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4bd340b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>You can't see the quick through a dark nail <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Instead, take off a little at a time and look at the cut end after each trim <sup><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Still safe:</strong> the center looks dry and flaky.</li><li><strong>Getting close to the quick:</strong> you see a chalky white ring <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>, or the center starts to look shiny and moist, a bit like the inside of a jellybean <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c701e91", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Stop as soon as you see that change <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a><a href=\"#s6\" aria-label=\"Source 6\">[6]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9bd960b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If you've never trimmed nails before, ask your vet or a vet tech to show you how <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "8f70677", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "2b3137b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Trimming step by step", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "trimming-step-by-step"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "45eb9f2", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "1", "right": "1", "bottom": "1", "left": "1", "isLinked": true}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder"}}, "elements": [{"id": "7c642e9", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What you'll need</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Nail clippers or a nail grinder made for dogs <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup></li><li>Styptic powder, or cornstarch, in case a nail bleeds <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup></li><li>Treats</li><li>Good light</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "32ce712", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Choosing a clipper or grinder? See <a href=\"/dog-grooming-tools/\">choosing clippers or a grinder</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9f6a82d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<ol><li><strong>Get comfortable.</strong> Your dog can sit or lie beside you, on your lap or on a non-slip surface, wherever they're settled <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Hold the paw gently but firmly.</strong> Put your thumb on the pad of a toe and your forefinger on the skin above the nail <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Move any fur out of the way</strong> so you can see the whole nail <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Extend the nail:</strong> push your thumb slightly up and back on the pad while pushing your forefinger forward <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Clip only the tip, straight across</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Don't clip past the point where the nail curves down <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Check the cut end</strong> before taking any more, especially on dark nails. See <a href=\"#finding-the-quick\">Finding the quick</a> above.</li><li><strong>Give a treat, then move to the next nail.</strong> You don't have to do every nail in one go.</li></ol>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "512838d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Dewclaws", "header_size": "h3"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e8453fe", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If your dog has dewclaws, the nails higher up on the inner side of the paw, include them when you trim <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Use the same method: hold the toe, extend the nail, and clip only the tip.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "497ad65", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "56f0ce1", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Stop and see your vet</strong> if a nail is cracked, split, torn or broken, or the toe is swollen, red, has discharge, or your dog is licking it or limping. Don't try to trim around an injury.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "4142421", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If your dog is older and finds standing or holding a paw up difficult, see <a href=\"/senior-dog-grooming/\">nail care for older dogs</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "190cad4", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "157c8f5", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Grinder or clipper?", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "grinder-or-clipper"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c37dd04", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Both are safe when used correctly. Some dogs tolerate a grinder better, while others prefer clippers <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "d43ad44", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<div class=\"gd-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\">Clippers</th><th scope=\"col\">Grinder</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>How it works</strong></th><td>Cuts the tip off in one squeeze</td><td>Wears the nail down a little at a time <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Things to know</strong></th><td>Guillotine-style clippers have a single blade. Some veterinary guidance advises against them because they can crush the nail rather than cut it cleanly <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>. Scissor- or plier-style clippers, where two blades cross, avoid this <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</td><td>Makes noise, which some dogs find frightening <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup>. Grinding too long in one spot can heat the nail and make your dog uncomfortable, so use short touches <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><strong>Often suits</strong></th><td>Quick, routine trims</td><td>Thicker nails, or dogs that dislike the feel of clippers <sup><a href=\"#s5\" aria-label=\"Source 5\">[5]</a></sup></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "b85dd2f", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Using a grinder safely</strong> <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>:</p>\n<ul><li>Use a grinder made for dogs.</li><li>Grind only a small part of the nail at a time.</li><li>Support the toe firmly but gently.</li><li>Grind across the bottom of the nail, then carefully in from the tip, smoothing rough edges.</li><li>Hold the grinder higher up, toward the top, for better control.</li><li>If your dog has long hair, hold it back so it can't get caught in the grinder.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "061a995", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Keep clippers handy even if you usually grind. You may need them for an area the grinder can't reach <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "9ab1e44", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>For which specific tool to buy, see <a href=\"/dog-grooming-tools/\">choosing clippers or a grinder</a>.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "63b3975", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "d14fbb1", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "If you cut the quick", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "if-you-cut-the-quick"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "c6197f9", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "752b236", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Nicking the quick happens, even to careful owners. Your dog will probably yelp and may pull away <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>.</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Stay calm,</strong> and keep hold of the paw if you can do so safely.</li><li><strong>Apply styptic powder or cornstarch</strong> to the bleeding nail tip straight away. Press gently so it sticks <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Give it a few minutes.</strong> A cut quick may bleed for a few minutes. It can be briefly painful <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Leave the rest of the nails for another day</strong> if your dog is upset.</li></ol>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}, {"id": "5c625b4", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 8, "column": "8", "row": "8", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "24", "right": "24", "bottom": "24", "left": "24", "isLinked": true}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "16", "right": "16", "bottom": "16", "left": "16", "isLinked": true}, "border_radius": {"unit": "px", "top": "8", "right": "8", "bottom": "8", "left": "8", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#FBF8F3", "border_border": "solid", "border_width": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "4", "isLinked": false}, "border_color": "#8A5A00", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfw", "border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdwarn"}}, "elements": [{"id": "50fb9c0", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Call your vet</strong> if the bleeding hasn't stopped after a few minutes <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup>, or if the nail looks damaged.</p>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "d3e0494", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "267b9cd", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Shortening overgrown nails", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "shortening-overgrown-nails"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "1732c9d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>If the nails have been left to grow, you can't cut them back to a short length in one session.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "08c135b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>Why:</strong> the quick grows along with the nail. Regular trimming helps it recede from the end <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Once a nail and its quick have grown long, though, there's a limit to how much can be trimmed back at once <sup><a href=\"#s3\" aria-label=\"Source 3\">[3]</a></sup>.</p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e45eb71", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p><strong>What to do:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Trim little and often:</strong> take off just the tip each time, stopping before the quick, and repeat on a regular schedule (see <a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\">how often to trim nails</a>). Over time the quick shortens with the nail <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</li><li><strong>Don't try to fix it in one go.</strong> Cutting deep enough to reach the quick will hurt your dog and make them wary of the next trim.</li><li><strong>Get help</strong> if the nails are very overgrown, curling, or you can't see where to stop. Your vet or a groomer can help.</li></ul>"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "e67992b", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "c43797c", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Common questions", "header_size": "h2", "_element_id": "common-questions"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "f5c3335", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "accordion", "settings": {"tabs": [{"_id": "7f59b52", "tab_title": "How short should my dog's nails be?", "tab_content": "<p>Short enough that they don't touch the ground when your dog walks <sup><a href=\"#s4\" aria-label=\"Source 4\">[4]</a></sup> and you don't hear them clicking on hard floors <sup><a href=\"#s2\" aria-label=\"Source 2\">[2]</a></sup>. When you trim, take only the tip, straight across, and stop before the quick <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>.</p>"}, {"_id": "5358aa3", "tab_title": "Does walking on pavement file a dog's nails down?", "tab_content": "<p>It can help. Some dogs wear their nails down and won't need trimming as often <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. Many still need regular trims, though, so keep checking for clicking and length rather than relying on walks alone.</p>"}, {"_id": "30a8625", "tab_title": "Can I use human nail clippers on my dog?", "tab_content": "<p>It's best to use clippers or a grinder made for dogs <sup><a href=\"#s1\" aria-label=\"Source 1\">[1]</a></sup>. They're designed for the shape and thickness of a dog's nail. See <a href=\"/dog-grooming-tools/\">choosing clippers or a grinder</a>.</p>"}], "title_html_tag": "h3", "faq_schema": "yes", "selected_icon": {"value": "fas fa-plus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "selected_active_icon": {"value": "fas fa-minus", "library": "fa-solid"}, "border_color": "#D9E0E4", "title_color": "#17324D", "tab_active_color": "#17324D", "__globals__": {"border_color": "globals/colors?id=gdborder", "title_color": "globals/colors?id=primary", "tab_active_color": "globals/colors?id=primary"}}, "elements": []}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "bba2096", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 760, "sizes": []}, "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "48", "right": "24", "bottom": "48", "left": "24", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "32", "right": "16", "bottom": "32", "left": "16", "isLinked": false}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#F5F7F8", "__globals__": {"background_color": "globals/colors?id=gdsurfs"}}, "elements": [{"id": "c1a4b80", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p class=\"gd-label\" id=\"next\"><strong>Where to go next</strong></p>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "504ab15", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "row", "flex_wrap": "wrap", "flex_direction_mobile": "column", "flex_gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 16, "colu